1
00:00:23,899 --> 00:00:26,999
It's raining on and off.

2
00:00:26,999 --> 00:00:28,039
Right.

3
00:00:28,039 --> 00:00:29,709
(It's pouring down, breaking through the summer heat.)

4
00:00:29,769 --> 00:00:30,909
A subtropical climate?

5
00:00:30,909 --> 00:00:32,709
I guess it's turning into that.

6
00:00:33,709 --> 00:00:36,509
So we were supposed to film outdoors today.

7
00:00:36,709 --> 00:00:37,979
The staff set everything up.

8
00:00:38,149 --> 00:00:40,179
- It's pouring down.
- We had to pivot abruptly.

9
00:00:40,179 --> 00:00:42,849
That's why we're filming inside a cafe.

10
00:00:42,949 --> 00:00:44,449
But as soon as we started filming,

11
00:00:44,449 --> 00:00:46,819
it stopped raining.

12
00:00:46,819 --> 00:00:47,889
- Right.
- Look.

13
00:00:48,189 --> 00:00:51,059
(It was pouring down like this earlier.)

14
00:00:51,229 --> 00:00:52,929
This is one of those toughest days.

15
00:00:52,929 --> 00:00:54,259
- Right. But it'd start raining...
- Yes.

16
00:00:54,329 --> 00:00:56,399
- once we step out.
- Right.

17
00:00:56,599 --> 00:00:58,269
We're in Gwangjin-gu. Right?

18
00:00:58,269 --> 00:01:00,439
I used to live in Gwangjin-gu.

19
00:01:00,569 --> 00:01:01,839
- Really?
- Yes.

20
00:01:01,839 --> 00:01:02,869
I see. When?

21
00:01:02,869 --> 00:01:04,239
When I was attending Sejong University.

22
00:01:04,709 --> 00:01:06,509
(It's located in Gunja-dong, Gwangjin-gu.)

23
00:01:06,739 --> 00:01:07,739
Listen.

24
00:01:08,479 --> 00:01:09,549
- I understand...
- Well...

25
00:01:09,549 --> 00:01:12,049
- that you love your alma mater.
- No, listen.

26
00:01:12,649 --> 00:01:14,349
He's always mentioning the university.

27
00:01:14,949 --> 00:01:18,019
Seriously. The university ought to give him an award.

28
00:01:18,089 --> 00:01:19,959
The university is pleased with it.

29
00:01:20,659 --> 00:01:24,029
So they told me a bit about today's guests.

30
00:01:24,459 --> 00:01:26,099
- I didn't know about the guests.
- Okay.

31
00:01:26,299 --> 00:01:28,029
But my stylist told me about them.

32
00:01:28,029 --> 00:01:29,569
- So you heard?
- Yes.

33
00:01:29,599 --> 00:01:32,599
Their stylist picked up an outfit that was set aside for our show.

34
00:01:32,599 --> 00:01:33,939
I see. The stylists...

35
00:01:33,939 --> 00:01:35,539
- went to pick up the outfits.
- Yes, it was during the pick-up.

36
00:01:35,569 --> 00:01:37,609
My stylist glanced over...

37
00:01:37,609 --> 00:01:40,039
and saw someone pick up the outfit that was set aside for our show.

38
00:01:40,279 --> 00:01:41,439
My stylist saw the name too.

39
00:01:41,609 --> 00:01:43,649
I didn't try to find out, but I ended up finding out anyway.

40
00:01:43,649 --> 00:01:44,979
She was in "Teach You a Lesson."

41
00:01:44,979 --> 00:01:47,149
- I really liked that drama.
- My gosh.

42
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:49,289
- Jin Ki Joo.
- It's Ki Joo.

43
00:01:49,289 --> 00:01:52,059
Yes. I really enjoyed watching her drama.

44
00:01:52,689 --> 00:01:54,559
Wait. Is she coming now?

45
00:01:54,589 --> 00:01:56,559
Is she? Who's that? Ki Joo is coming?

46
00:01:57,259 --> 00:01:59,159
So have you guys made a lot of headway with the filming?

47
00:01:59,329 --> 00:02:01,299
Yes. We made a lot of headway with it.

48
00:02:01,299 --> 00:02:04,469
And the director tends to shoot the scenes quite fast.

49
00:02:04,629 --> 00:02:05,869
That's amazing.

50
00:02:06,539 --> 00:02:07,739
I think it's Ki Joo.

51
00:02:07,999 --> 00:02:09,309
One of them is Ki Joo.

52
00:02:09,309 --> 00:02:10,339
But who's the other one?

53
00:02:13,339 --> 00:02:14,379
My gosh.

54
00:02:15,079 --> 00:02:16,109
Isn't that Cha Tae Hyun?

55
00:02:16,579 --> 00:02:18,449
- I think it's Tae Hyun.
- It's Cha Tae Hyun again.

56
00:02:18,449 --> 00:02:19,849
- Come on.
- Tae Hyun.

57
00:02:19,979 --> 00:02:21,719
He's joining us again.

58
00:02:22,419 --> 00:02:24,019
It's Tae Hyun again.

59
00:02:24,019 --> 00:02:25,019
(Chuckling)

60
00:02:25,089 --> 00:02:26,659
- CEO Cha.
- My gosh.

61
00:02:27,359 --> 00:02:28,619
- Ki Joo.
- Hello.

62
00:02:28,619 --> 00:02:30,629
- I brought her to round things out.
- Hello, Ki Joo.

63
00:02:30,629 --> 00:02:32,059
- I see.
- Okay.

64
00:02:34,199 --> 00:02:37,069
(He's been on the show for every season!)

65
00:02:38,299 --> 00:02:41,269
(Every time he came on, they made it to Round 3,)

66
00:02:41,269 --> 00:02:45,009
(and he always boosted the ratings.)

67
00:02:45,239 --> 00:02:47,739
(The show's loving Whenever Friend, Cha Tae Hyun)

68
00:02:48,509 --> 00:02:50,709
(She shot to national fame... with her role...)

69
00:02:50,709 --> 00:02:52,949
(in a weekend drama, "Homemade Love Story.")

70
00:02:53,879 --> 00:02:57,449
(She pulled off her characters in romantic comedies...)

71
00:02:57,449 --> 00:03:00,459
(and nailed the action scenes to perfection.)

72
00:03:00,859 --> 00:03:04,289
(The fully versatile actress, Jin Ki Joo)

73
00:03:04,629 --> 00:03:08,229
(The 1st actress at CEO Cha's agency)

74
00:03:08,359 --> 00:03:09,699
- Hello.
- Hello.

75
00:03:09,699 --> 00:03:11,169
- I brought her too.
- Tae Hyun's agency...

76
00:03:11,169 --> 00:03:13,299
- signed Ki Joo.
- That's right.

77
00:03:13,299 --> 00:03:14,339
- Ki Joo.
- I know.

78
00:03:14,339 --> 00:03:16,439
- How did you end up at his agency?
- You...

79
00:03:16,439 --> 00:03:17,809
You brought an actress to our show.

80
00:03:17,839 --> 00:03:19,609
- I'm here as her manager.
- I mean...

81
00:03:19,709 --> 00:03:20,979
- My gosh.
- All right. Let's sit down.

82
00:03:20,979 --> 00:03:22,109
- Sit there, Ki Joo.
- Tae Hyun is here again.

83
00:03:22,109 --> 00:03:23,109
- By the way, - Yes.

84
00:03:23,909 --> 00:03:27,419
Ki Joo joined the agency Tae Hyun and In Sung are running.

85
00:03:27,419 --> 00:03:28,449
That's right.

86
00:03:28,449 --> 00:03:30,219
- She signed with their agency.
- I mean... Yes.

87
00:03:30,249 --> 00:03:32,159
Her drama, "Teach You a Lesson," was a huge hit.

88
00:03:32,159 --> 00:03:33,719
- Right.
- Actually...

89
00:03:33,759 --> 00:03:35,059
- You know what?
- It happened...

90
00:03:35,059 --> 00:03:36,429
- I...
- right after you signed her.

91
00:03:36,429 --> 00:03:38,459
I'm such a lucky guy.

92
00:03:40,029 --> 00:03:41,729
Will I stay lucky until I die?

93
00:03:42,129 --> 00:03:44,299
- How could this happen?
- Tae Hyun, you're such a lucky guy.

94
00:03:44,299 --> 00:03:45,329
- Seriously.
- I agree.

95
00:03:45,329 --> 00:03:46,699
It seems he's luckier than he is hardworking.

96
00:03:46,699 --> 00:03:48,469
- Seriously.
- I mean it.

97
00:03:48,539 --> 00:03:51,369
On top of that, when Bo Pil invited me to the show,

98
00:03:52,039 --> 00:03:54,739
he said I was like the show's lucky charm.

99
00:03:55,709 --> 00:03:58,379
It's my first time joining a show...

100
00:03:58,409 --> 00:03:59,719
as its lucky charm.

101
00:03:59,779 --> 00:04:02,789
So I'm practically the pig's head for this show.

102
00:04:03,219 --> 00:04:04,289
That's how it feels.

103
00:04:04,549 --> 00:04:06,689
- You're right.
- I guess it's like a ritual.

104
00:04:06,689 --> 00:04:08,359
- It was so funny.
- Tae Hyun...

105
00:04:08,519 --> 00:04:10,389
has to join us every season.

106
00:04:10,389 --> 00:04:11,859
- He helps our season succeed.
- Yes.

107
00:04:11,859 --> 00:04:13,459
- But the timing was great.
- Okay.

108
00:04:13,659 --> 00:04:16,199
It's crazy. I'm so lucky.

109
00:04:16,199 --> 00:04:17,429
(Lady Luck must be on my side.)

110
00:04:17,599 --> 00:04:20,039
- I filmed a drama last year.
- Okay.

111
00:04:20,039 --> 00:04:21,039
It's a short one.

112
00:04:21,039 --> 00:04:22,309
- It has eight episodes.
- What about it?

113
00:04:22,669 --> 00:04:25,369
It's going to premiere in September.

114
00:04:25,509 --> 00:04:26,539
On SBS?

115
00:04:26,539 --> 00:04:27,939
No, on an online streaming platform.

116
00:04:28,039 --> 00:04:29,109
I see. But what about that?

117
00:04:29,109 --> 00:04:31,479
- This episode will air in August.
- That's right.

118
00:04:31,879 --> 00:04:33,549
- What a great PR chance.
- You can promote the drama.

119
00:04:33,549 --> 00:04:35,149
(He can promote the drama at the perfect timing.)

120
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:36,949
- It's called, "Your Personal Taxi."
- He sure is lucky.

121
00:04:36,949 --> 00:04:38,719
I'm a taxi driver in the drama.

122
00:04:38,719 --> 00:04:39,719
- Really?
- Yes.

123
00:04:39,719 --> 00:04:40,989
- He's so lucky.
- So...

124
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:42,019
to explain the plot...

125
00:04:42,019 --> 00:04:43,289
You guys can just add in the information.

126
00:04:43,289 --> 00:04:45,599
It's so complicated to describe the plot.

127
00:04:45,799 --> 00:04:48,129
(As you requested, we're adding this in.)

128
00:04:48,969 --> 00:04:50,969
(A feel-good music drama where a taxi driver listens to...)

129
00:04:50,969 --> 00:04:53,239
(his passengers' stories and comforts them)

130
00:04:53,699 --> 00:04:56,909
(Tae Hyun's upcoming drama will premiere soon.)

131
00:04:57,709 --> 00:04:58,879
Well, this worked out for me.

132
00:04:58,939 --> 00:04:59,939
Right, it did.

133
00:05:00,179 --> 00:05:01,809
It's an 8-episode series at 30 minutes each.

134
00:05:01,809 --> 00:05:03,249
- I want to talk to Ki Joo.
- It'll be short...

135
00:05:03,249 --> 00:05:04,509
- Right. Ki Joo.
- Exactly.

136
00:05:04,609 --> 00:05:06,249
I want to stop listening to you.

137
00:05:06,249 --> 00:05:08,119
- I want to talk to her.
- Okay.

138
00:05:08,179 --> 00:05:09,889
- Let's talk to her.
- Yes.

139
00:05:09,889 --> 00:05:11,149
- I saw you and Tae Hyun...
- Me? Great.

140
00:05:11,149 --> 00:05:12,659
walking toward us from a distance.

141
00:05:12,889 --> 00:05:14,719
At first, I didn't know you guys were celebrities.

142
00:05:14,719 --> 00:05:15,759
(They look like colleagues out for a stroll.)

143
00:05:15,829 --> 00:05:17,329
I wondered if you were out for a stroll.

144
00:05:17,329 --> 00:05:18,329
They were at ease.

145
00:05:18,329 --> 00:05:20,099
- They were walking at ease.
- Right.

146
00:05:20,099 --> 00:05:21,829
- They were so chill.
- That's right.

147
00:05:21,829 --> 00:05:24,129
- You guys seemed so relaxed.
- Actually, Ki Joo...

148
00:05:24,129 --> 00:05:25,969
- Yes.
- lives around here.

149
00:05:25,969 --> 00:05:27,269
- I see.
- I'm familiar with this place.

150
00:05:27,269 --> 00:05:28,299
This is her turf.

151
00:05:28,299 --> 00:05:29,869
- I finally got to hear her voice.
- Yes.

152
00:05:30,469 --> 00:05:32,239
- Is this like your hometown?
- Right.

153
00:05:32,239 --> 00:05:33,409
- Yes.
- Really?

154
00:05:33,409 --> 00:05:34,709
- Go on. Tell them.
- I come here...

155
00:05:34,709 --> 00:05:36,209
- for a walk.
- Around Guui?

156
00:05:36,209 --> 00:05:37,309
- I come here for a walk.
- Here?

157
00:05:37,309 --> 00:05:38,919
- This place is great.
- There's a mountain too.

158
00:05:38,919 --> 00:05:42,389
How long have you been living in Guui-dong?

159
00:05:42,449 --> 00:05:45,049
At the beginning of my acting career,

160
00:05:45,189 --> 00:05:46,859
my CEO used to live here.

161
00:05:46,859 --> 00:05:48,719
He recommended this neighborhood.

162
00:05:48,959 --> 00:05:50,229
I can easily go to beauty salons too.

163
00:05:50,229 --> 00:05:51,729
- Really?
- You just have to cross the river.

164
00:05:51,729 --> 00:05:53,229
You're talking about a different CEO, right?

165
00:05:53,229 --> 00:05:55,229
- Yes. There was another CEO.
- Another CEO.

166
00:05:55,599 --> 00:05:57,099
- She's with your agency now.
- Well,

167
00:05:57,099 --> 00:05:59,399
let me give you some context about this CEO.

168
00:05:59,669 --> 00:06:00,899
The CEO of her former agency...

169
00:06:00,899 --> 00:06:03,039
- used to be In Sung's manager.
- Was he...

170
00:06:03,039 --> 00:06:04,339
I see. Is that so?

171
00:06:04,339 --> 00:06:06,979
When In Sung and I set up the company, he brought them too.

172
00:06:06,979 --> 00:06:08,409
You joined their agency with the CEO too?

173
00:06:08,409 --> 00:06:09,509
- I see.
- Then...

174
00:06:09,509 --> 00:06:10,509
(That's how she joined his agency.)

175
00:06:10,579 --> 00:06:12,379
I can't believe I got so lucky.

176
00:06:12,449 --> 00:06:14,679
- Right. You...
- Jae Seok.

177
00:06:14,679 --> 00:06:16,389
Do you know what's crazy now?

178
00:06:16,389 --> 00:06:18,149
- I want to listen to her talk.
- Okay.

179
00:06:18,189 --> 00:06:20,659
- Earlier...
- You need to stop talking.

180
00:06:20,659 --> 00:06:21,759
I want to listen to her talk.

181
00:06:21,759 --> 00:06:23,889
He took over the conversation after talking about...

182
00:06:23,889 --> 00:06:25,759
- the former CEO.
- You can't give me an opening.

183
00:06:25,759 --> 00:06:26,829
- We can't give him an opening.
- Yes.

184
00:06:26,899 --> 00:06:28,459
Didn't a lot of people reach out...

185
00:06:28,459 --> 00:06:29,929
- after your drama aired?
- Gosh, it's hot.

186
00:06:30,099 --> 00:06:32,399
More people reached out to me than ever before.

187
00:06:32,569 --> 00:06:34,599
- He also texted me really fast.
- When...

188
00:06:34,599 --> 00:06:35,809
- Really?
- Yes.

189
00:06:36,009 --> 00:06:37,369
Right. After "Teach You a Lesson,"

190
00:06:37,809 --> 00:06:39,679
she got so many offers...

191
00:06:39,679 --> 00:06:41,179
- for new roles. Okay.
- I want to hear it from her.

192
00:06:42,279 --> 00:06:43,509
- Okay.
- We can't stop talking.

193
00:06:43,509 --> 00:06:45,109
- I'll hear it from her.
- This is why.

194
00:06:45,179 --> 00:06:46,679
We have to keep the conversation going.

195
00:06:46,679 --> 00:06:48,849
Ki Joo, you need to teach him a lesson.

196
00:06:48,849 --> 00:06:49,889
- Right.
- Gosh, no.

197
00:06:49,889 --> 00:06:51,189
"Do not talk."

198
00:06:51,249 --> 00:06:53,659
- Right. Teach him a lesson.
- Yes.

199
00:06:54,819 --> 00:06:56,689
- You got many offers.
- What should I say?

200
00:06:57,229 --> 00:06:58,589
- Yes, I got many offers.
- Right.

201
00:06:58,589 --> 00:07:00,159
My friends also congratulated me.

202
00:07:00,159 --> 00:07:01,829
Even people I haven't talked to for years congratulated me.

203
00:07:01,829 --> 00:07:03,829
- They reached out to you.
- I see.

204
00:07:04,229 --> 00:07:06,369
You and Yeon Seok have never worked on a project together.

205
00:07:06,369 --> 00:07:07,739
- Right. We never worked together.
- Right. Probably not.

206
00:07:07,739 --> 00:07:08,869
You guys have never met before?

207
00:07:08,969 --> 00:07:11,239
- We met at awards ceremonies.
- That's right.

208
00:07:11,239 --> 00:07:12,579
- Really?
- Yes.

209
00:07:12,909 --> 00:07:14,439
- Gosh, awards ceremonies.
- What?

210
00:07:14,439 --> 00:07:16,579
Yeon Seok starred in the drama,

211
00:07:16,579 --> 00:07:19,379
- "Phantom Lawyer" this year.
- Yes.

212
00:07:19,449 --> 00:07:21,049
- He did a fantastic job.
- Right. He was great.

213
00:07:21,049 --> 00:07:22,689
I really enjoyed watching the drama.

214
00:07:23,289 --> 00:07:24,349
Because of "Agent Kim Reactivated,"

215
00:07:25,289 --> 00:07:28,059
- he won't get any awards this year.
- Hey.

216
00:07:28,489 --> 00:07:30,229
- Why...
- Ji Sub totally killed it.

217
00:07:30,229 --> 00:07:32,089
Why are you bringing that up now?

218
00:07:32,089 --> 00:07:33,459
- Tae Hyun.
- He'll win the Grand Award.

219
00:07:34,429 --> 00:07:35,459
- I...
- Come on.

220
00:07:35,459 --> 00:07:36,499
I never thought I could win...

221
00:07:36,499 --> 00:07:37,569
- the Grand Award.
- Listen.

222
00:07:37,569 --> 00:07:39,399
- But it is a bummer.
- What do you mean?

223
00:07:39,639 --> 00:07:41,769
- The ceremony hasn't even...
- You did a great job.

224
00:07:41,769 --> 00:07:43,839
- It hasn't even started. Stop that.
- There's no mention of that now.

225
00:07:43,869 --> 00:07:46,279
- How could he be so unlucky?
- You know what?

226
00:07:46,939 --> 00:07:48,639
"Phantom Lawyer" did well too.

227
00:07:48,639 --> 00:07:49,749
Exactly.

228
00:07:49,749 --> 00:07:51,279
I might not have a shot with the year-end awards ceremony.

229
00:07:51,279 --> 00:07:53,449
But I did win an award at an SBS awards ceremony.

230
00:07:53,449 --> 00:07:55,179
I think they gave it to me proactively.

231
00:07:55,419 --> 00:07:57,619
Then they don't want you to come to the awards ceremony.

232
00:07:58,449 --> 00:07:59,459
(A spot-on analysis)

233
00:07:59,459 --> 00:08:00,559
My gosh.

234
00:08:00,559 --> 00:08:01,719
They already handled it.

235
00:08:01,719 --> 00:08:02,859
Nominating him would be tough too.

236
00:08:02,859 --> 00:08:05,429
Do you collect gossip about our industry...

237
00:08:06,359 --> 00:08:08,329
and spread it?

238
00:08:08,329 --> 00:08:09,869
- Hey.
- Gossip about the TV industry?

239
00:08:09,869 --> 00:08:10,869
Gosh, that's a great way to handle it.

240
00:08:10,869 --> 00:08:12,599
- They already gave me an award.
- This guy...

241
00:08:12,599 --> 00:08:14,099
That's the Grand Award for the first half of this year.

242
00:08:14,099 --> 00:08:15,299
So...

243
00:08:16,469 --> 00:08:17,839
That's the Grand Award for the first half of this year.

244
00:08:18,269 --> 00:08:19,709
Hang in there for the next season.

245
00:08:19,709 --> 00:08:20,739
- I see.
- I see.

246
00:08:21,309 --> 00:08:23,279
We received some snacks for product replacement today.

247
