469
00:15:32,669 --> 00:15:33,679
My sister-in-law.

470
00:15:35,009 --> 00:15:36,009
Your sister-in-law?

471
00:15:36,009 --> 00:15:37,579
She told me it was really fun.

472
00:15:37,579 --> 00:15:39,449
She said playing pickleball was really fun.

473
00:15:39,449 --> 00:15:40,779
Where's your sister-in-law?

474
00:15:41,119 --> 00:15:43,419
She plays somewhere else. We don't play together.

475
00:15:44,989 --> 00:15:45,989
Right.

476
00:15:45,989 --> 00:15:47,519
(A wise decision for both of their sakes)

477
00:15:47,519 --> 00:15:48,859
- I see. Right.
- It won't be easy.

478
00:15:48,859 --> 00:15:50,489
Playing together might be too much.

479
00:15:50,559 --> 00:15:51,889
It might be too much.

480
00:15:51,889 --> 00:15:55,459
What's so fun about pickleball?

481
00:15:55,459 --> 00:15:57,969
You're willing to put aside time to play pickleball.

482
00:15:57,969 --> 00:16:00,069
People who can't run well like me can still play.

483
00:16:00,069 --> 00:16:01,299
- Really?
- Yes.

484
00:16:01,299 --> 00:16:04,339
When I tried it out for the first time, it was so fun.

485
00:16:04,339 --> 00:16:06,339
There isn't a place I can play this in my neighborhood.

486
00:16:06,339 --> 00:16:08,009
I take the bus to come here. It takes an hour.

487
00:16:08,809 --> 00:16:10,609
- She's so diligent.
- Sweating it out doesn't tire you.

488
00:16:10,609 --> 00:16:12,049
- It actually boosts your energy.
- Yes.

489
00:16:12,049 --> 00:16:14,249
- Right. It energizes me.
- That's true.

490
00:16:14,249 --> 00:16:15,579
(It chases away fatigue and boosts their energy.)

491
00:16:15,579 --> 00:16:17,489
You wrote you would bond for an hour while playing together...

492
00:16:17,489 --> 00:16:19,419
- and then drift apart.
- You wrote you'd drift apart then.

493
00:16:19,419 --> 00:16:20,419
- That's right.
- What does that mean?

494
